# MediCare Scheduler – Global Cursor Rules
# ---------------------------------------

## Context
Internal healthcare scheduler built with:
• Next.js (App Router)  • TypeScript strict
• Tailwind CSS  • Supabase (PostgreSQL + Storage)
• FullCalendar (Month/Week/Day)  • Google Maps (Map view)

Staff management exists in-app; staff do not need to log in for v1.

## Explicit Non-Goals (v1)
- No driver assignment
- No transportation workflows
- No dispatching / route optimization

## Code-Style Standards
- TypeScript `strict: true`; prefer `const` and explicit return types
- camelCase for vars/fns, PascalCase for React components
- Semicolons on, trailing commas on
- Use Tailwind utility classes; never inline `<style>`
- One React component per file; co-locate hooks alongside component if shared

## Supabase Patterns
- Always import the pre-configured client from `/lib/supabase.ts`
- Queried columns must be explicit:  
  `supabase.from('patients').select('id, name, phone')`
- Check `error` on every response – throw or surface a toast
- Use UUID PKs; store flexible fields in `custom_fields` JSONB
- No RLS (single-user), but keep `service_role_key` server-side only
- Storage uploads return signed URLs valid ≤ 1 hour

## Google Calendar Integration (optional)
- Not required for v1; implement only after core scheduling UI is stable
- Event title template: `[First] - [Area] - [Type] - [Staff Firsts]`
- Time-zone always `Asia/Dubai`; format dates `DD/MM/YYYY`
- Handle Google webhook `event.updated` → patch DB row

## React / UI Rules
- Use FullCalendar React with 15-min slot duration
- Drag-&-drop reschedules appointment & triggers calendar patch
- All forms use React Hook Form + Zod; surface field errors inline
- Copy-Appointment modal must deep-clone appointment (new UUID, events)

## Error & Loading UX
- `Skeleton` component for table & calendar placeholders
- Global error boundary logs to console and toast "Something went wrong"
- Wrap async calls with `try/catch`; show toast on error

## Testing
- Jest + React Testing Library for components
- Supabase queries mocked with `@supabase/supabase-js` stubs
- Calendar integration tests mock Google API responses

## Rule Metadata
ruleType: always
applyTo: "*"
